      "claim_changes": []
    },
    {
      "id": "2026-08-28-answerable-challenge-service",
      "date": "2026-08-28",
      "project": "normativity.legitimacy",
      "path": "projects/normativity/legitimacy/rounds/2026-08-28-answerable-challenge-service",
      "verdict": "CHALLENGE-CONTINUITY-SURVIVES-SERVICE-IS-THE-NEW-CONTENT — the registered challenge is the right object between criticism and promoted reason, and pinning its adjudication terms defeats the moving-goalpost attack: the same trace that never promotes anything under a threshold moving from 10 to 100 to 1000 promotes at t=11 when the episode's terms are fixed at registration, with the two fixtures differing in exactly one flag. Pinning binds the episode rather than the process, so prospective revision stays available and moving an open challenge onto new terms requires an explicit transfer, which frozen carry already expresses. The continuity half is nearly free and is frozen A1 for the third round running, which the document says in three places rather than presenting as discovery. The genuinely new mathematical burden is service: a challenge left open forever with opportunity recurring forever and nothing ever served satisfies every premise in this round and in the frozen package, because an outstanding claim nothing is done about is exactly what A1 is content with. The round does not solve self-sealing and says so: a general rule installed before any challenge, holding that criticisms threatening authority are rejected, is temporally clean and inferentially relevant and every structural condition here accepts it, and no premise was added to make it fail because every candidate considered would also have refused a legitimate resource-priority deferral. The outer boundary is an indistinguishability observation rather than a theorem: no predicate over represented history separates a world with no criticism from one whose decisive criticism was never registered.",
      "verdict_source": "projects/normativity/legitimacy/rounds/2026-08-28-answerable-challenge-service/README.md",
      "depends_on": [
